 every set $A$?","options":["Because there is no element of $\\varnothing$ that could fail to belong to $A$","Because every set $A$ contains $\\varnothing$ as one of its elements, listed or not.","Because $A$ must have at least one element","Because $\\varnothing$ and $A$ have the same elements"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"40f0cc6da9ec951b4b3e097a","time_limit":35},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q09_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $A=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{N}\\colon x<0\\}$ and $B=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\colon x^2+1=0\\}$. Which statement is true?","options":["$A=B$","$A\\neq B$, since $A$ is built from $\\mathbb{N}$ and $B$ from $\\mathbb{R}$","$A\\subseteq B$ but $A\\neq B$","$A$ and $B$ cannot be compared, since they have no elements"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b723422113fdc9fc6e5e5cec","time_limit":35},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q10_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which pair of identities holds for every set $A$?","options":["$A\\cup\\varnothing=A$ and $A\\cap\\varnothing=\\varnothing$","$A\\cup\\varnothing=\\varnothing$ and $A\\cap\\varnothing=A$","$A\\cup\\varnothing=A$ and $A\\cap\\varnothing=A$","$A\\cup\\varnothing=\\varnothing$ and $A\\cap\\varnothing=\\varnothing$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9cc7b0188feb342a04b8a20b","time_limit":25},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q15_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement correctly distinguishes $\\varnothing\\subseteq A$ from $\\varnothing\\in A$?","options":["$\\varnothing\\subseteq A$ is always true, but $\\varnothing\\in A$ depends on $A$.","$\\varnothing\\in A$ is always true, but $\\varnothing\\subseteq A$ depends on $A$.","Both are always true for every set $A$.","Both mean exactly the same thing."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e07baf44925df1e0ccc3f243","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-1a-math-i-calculus-empty-set-html-q16_curated20261027_004","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $B\\subseteq\\varnothing$, what must be true?","options":["$B=\\{\\varnothing\\}$","$B$ has exactly one element","$\\varnothing\\in B$","$B=\\varnothing$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"94b89099311267d738c7f67c","time_limit":30}]}}